and how you're gonna meet it.

260
00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:41.910
And it just doesn't work that way.

261
00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:42.760
No.

262
00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:47.187
So with all this anxiety and uncertainty,

263
00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:53.213
I stand in the ocean and I take my first step.

264
00:11:54.371 --> 00:11:56.430
And step one is take one step, right.

265
00:11:56.430 --> 00:11:58.560
Step one is take one step.

266
00:11:58.560 --> 00:11:59.770
And I keep walking.

267
00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:03.470
I walk across the lush fields of New Jersey.

268
00:12:03.470 --> 00:12:06.550
I walk across coal country in Pennsylvania

269
00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:08.903
where I share the road with Amish buggies.

270
00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:12.360
I see a double rainbow in Ohio.

271
00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:15.830
I started to develop like horrible plantar fasciitis,

272
00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:17.657
which I'm sure you're no stranger to,

273
00:12:17.657 --> 00:12:20.420
And like I wake up in the morning

274
00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:23.449
and I can like barely stand up.

275
00:12:23.449 --> 00:12:25.230
But I keep going anyways.

276
00:12:25.230 --> 00:12:28.860
I walk across Indiana, Illinois.

277
00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:31.110
I walk into Missouri during a heat wave

278
00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:33.220
where, you know, like the weatherman is on TV

279
00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:34.787
saying, stay inside.

280
00:12:34.787 --> 00:12:36.752
I'm like, screw it, I'm gonna walk 24.

281
00:12:36.752 --> 00:12:39.303
I'm walking usually 24 miles a day.

282
00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:46.100
I walk into Kansas, I walk across Kansas

283
00:12:48.070 --> 00:12:52.550
where I just saw unbelievable shooting stars

284
00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:57.550
and like orange sherbet sunrises every morning behind me

285
00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:00.210
that are so beautiful

286
00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:02.350
that I'm turning around to walk backwards.

287
00:13:02.350 --> 00:13:04.540
I'm walking to Colorado.

288
00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:09.540
And I've walked 1,797 miles at this point when, ahhh.

289
00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:14.697
I think what the, like pain shoots up my leg,

290
00:13:14.697 --> 00:13:16.547
and I'm like, what the heck was that.

291
00:13:17.740 --> 00:13:21.633
And then I hear a sound I don't wanna hear.

292
00:13:23.073 --> 00:13:25.106
(Mike mimics rattlesnake rattling)

293
00:13:25.106 --> 00:13:27.820
Then I realized that a poisonous rattlesnake

294
00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:32.173
just sunk its fangs into my left ankle.

295
00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:38.960
And at first I'm not thinking too much of it.

296
00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:40.750
I'm trying to just stay calm.

297
00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:44.810
But I glance around and there were two fans there

298
00:13:44.810 --> 00:13:48.600
that showed up to walk with me, but no gas station,

299
00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:56.610
no barns, no houses, not even any cows.

300
00:13:56.610 --> 00:13:57.983
Like this is bad.

301
00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:03.883
They call 911 and while they call 911,

302
00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:09.820
it was sort of like the end of Looney Tunes,

303
00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:10.653
if you remember that.

304
00:14:10.653 --> 00:14:11.881
Where it goes like this,

305
00:14:11.881 --> 00:14:14.340
the circles converge on the center of the screen

306
00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:16.390
and it says, that's all folks.

307
00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:18.900
Well, that's exactly what started to happening to me,

308
00:14:18.900 --> 00:14:23.050
except instead of colorful circles, it was darkness.

309
00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:25.060
And just, you know, blacks creeping in

310
00:14:25.060 --> 00:14:27.400
from the corners of my awareness

311
00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:29.893
and I could feel myself fading away.

312
00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:35.930
Now they let me speak to 911 and dispatch says,

313
00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:38.390
sir, I've sent an ambulance from two different towns

314
00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:41.333
and a helicopter, whatever gets there first, get in.

315
00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:45.243
And I asked, am I gonna die.

316
00:14:46.922 --> 00:14:51.713
And the voice on the other line says, I don't know, sir.

317
00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:59.140
I'm sitting there, I'm like this is not bee sting, you know.

318
00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:02.623
And an hour later, I'm in the back of an ambulance.

319
00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:13.220
It just dawns on me, like this could be the end of my life.

320
00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:15.123
This could be, hopefully not, you know.

321
00:15:15.123 --> 00:15:18.323
If they get me there, it all works out, but could not.

322
00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:23.120
And I just, I made a decision, Rich,

323
00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:27.960
that if indeed it is gonna be the end of my life,

324
00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:31.250
I'm not gonna waste it worrying

325
00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:32.680
about if it's the end of my life.

326
00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:34.650
Like, so I literally have this moment

327
00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:38.784
in the back of the ambulance where I'm just reclining.

328
00:15:38.784 --> 00:15:41.390
It almost felt like I was in some enlightened state.

329
00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:43.010
And right when I made that decision,

330
00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:46.740
I started to see, like the colors became more vibrant.

331
00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:48.980
And like I noticed this red paint

332
00:15:48.980 --> 00:15:50.650
on the back of the ambulance door,

333
00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:52.610
and it was like really red.

334
00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:55.470
It was beautiful and vibrant and alive.

335
00:15:55.470 --> 00:16:00.470
And there was just peace and everything made sense.

336
00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:13.590
Long story short, I go to the ICU for three days.

337
00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:14.423
I thought, you know,

338
00:16:14.423 --> 00:16:16.400
they have this medicine called antivenin.

339
00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:17.260
Right.

340
00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:18.093
And I thought-

341
00:16:18.093 --> 00:16:18.997
Just get the shot.

342
00:16:18.997 --> 00:16:20.920
Get back on the road.
I thought if I get that,

343
00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:22.180
'cause it's called antivenin,

344
00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:25.323
I thought I'd be walking the next day.

345
00:16:26.427 --> 00:16:27.310
It doesn't work like that.

346
00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:31.120
The antivenin just like makes it so you don't die, you know.

347
00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:33.650
But the doctor, you know, you're gonna be here while.

348
00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:34.660
Gotta watch your leg.

349
00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:37.900
And my leg swelled to like basically

350
00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:39.280
the size of an elephant trunk.

351
00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:41.194
Yeah, you shared photos of that on Instagram.

352
00:16:41.194 --> 00:16:42.340
Yeah, yeah.

353
00:16:42.340 --> 00:16:44.040
It was very haunting.

354
00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:47.580
Yeah, yeah, it got real big and real painful.

355
00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:51.000
And I went from walking 24 miles every day

356
00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:54.810
to like I couldn't walk to the bathroom without help.

357
00:16:54.810 --> 00:16:57.980
I had a walker and like somebody holding me.

358
00:16:57.980 --> 00:16:59.160
Relearning how to walk.

359
00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:01.270
I mean, were you in the hospital for five days or so?

360
00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:05.040
I was the hospital five days, ICU for three.

361
00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:10.040
And then, you know, due to amazing medical care

362
00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:12.350
at Park View Hospital in Colorado,

363
00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:13.863
I started to get better.

364
00:17:14.730 --> 00:17:18.905
And then actually came the hardest part of the snake bite.

365
00:17:18.905 --> 00:17:20.930
It wasn't actually getting bit by the snake.

366
00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:22.630
The hardest part of the snake bite

367
00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:26.190
was getting better from the snake bite

368
00:17:27.210 --> 00:17:30.711
because I went, after the hospital I wasn't ready to go.

369
00:17:30.711 --> 00:17:33.970
I basically had to rehab, took three weeks.

370
00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:35.711
Right, you went back to Michigan, right?

371
00:17:35.711 --> 00:17:36.544
That's right.

372
00:17:36.544 --> 00:17:37.377
Kinda heal up.

373
00:17:37.377 --> 00:17:38.230
That's right.

374
00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:42.383
And while I was there, everyone is like coddling me,

375
00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:49.750
cooking for me, wishing me well, you know.

376
00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:51.100
They're putting me on the news.

377
00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:55.470
John Mayer's DMing me on Instagram saying speedy recovery.

378
00:17:55.470 --> 00:18:00.470
I'm in like this nest of cuddly sympathetic softness.

379
00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:02.263
Right.

380
00:18:02.263 --> 00:18:03.096
And-

381
00:18:03.096 --> 00:18:04.570
The idea of putting yourself back

382
00:18:04.570 --> 00:18:07.870
into that difficult situation becomes all the harder.

383
00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:08.703
It's horrible.

384
00:18:08.703 --> 00:18:09.536
After the break.

385
00:18:09.536 --> 00:18:13.970
And yeah, three weeks and I just can't deny it any longer.

386
00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:15.683
My ankle was healed.

387
00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:21.860
And so, I'm looking at the map and I have 1000,

388
00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:25.700
you know, that's 38 marathons.

389
00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:29.113
I have 1000 hot, horrible miles left.

390
00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:33.580
And I gotta decide like,

391
00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:36.380
just like when I walked into the table and got hurt before,

392
00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:38.420
like I have another reason.

393
00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:40.600
This is a great reason actually,

394
00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:45.082
because if I quit, no one will even think I'm a quitter.

395
00:18:45.082 --> 00:18:46.970
They're like, hey, I almost died.

396
00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:48.803
It wasn't meant to be, whatever.

397
00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:56.730
But I started to realize like 99 times out of 100,

398
00:18:57.970 --> 00:19:01.550
my reasons are just excuses wearing fancy clothes.

399
00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:03.220
That's it, they're the same.

400
00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:05.410
Reason, excuse, it's the same thing.

401
00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:08.750
So I gotta decide like, am I gonna live my life

402
00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:13.750
according to my excuses slash reasons or to my commitment.

403
00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:19.800
And I said, screw it, man, I'mma go back out there.

404
00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:21.610
I got like the sweltering heat.

405
00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:23.330
I got that horrible foot pain.

406
00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:27.330
I got the snake riddled roads of Colorado 10.

407
00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:28.500
They're waiting for me, in fact,

408
00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:30.350
like basically hell's waiting for me.

409
00:19:31.764 --> 00:19:35.457
And it's like, screw it.

410
00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:39.420
You know, I wanna meet to hell too, let's go.

411
00:19:39.420 --> 00:19:40.940
So I go back to the exact spot.

412
00:19:40.940 --> 00:19:41.773
And I was like scared, man.

413
00:19:41.773 --> 00:19:43.750
I was having like nightmares about snakes.

414
00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:46.140
I still don't like snakes, you know.

415
00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:48.266
I didn't wanna go back to that spot, you know.

416
00:19:48.266 --> 00:19:49.950
Yeah, of course.

417
00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:51.470
It was scary.

418
00:19:51.470 --> 00:19:53.360
The PTSD of it.

419
00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:54.260
It was scary.

420
00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:55.670
What's interesting is,

421
00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:59.340
to kind of create a little bit more context for this,

422
00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:01.460
the whole idea behind the walk.

423
00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:04.000
I mean, I know there's this kind of origin story.

424
00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:05.760
You were in a Teeny's jewelry shop

425
00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:08.847
and somebody had mentioned that they had a friend who did it

426
00:20:08.847 --> 00:20:11.130
and that kind of planted the seed.

427
00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:13.810
But the seed is germinated over the course

428
00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:15.990
of you completing this album

429
00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:17.670
and being faced with the prospect

430
00:20:17.670 --> 00:20:21.150
of having to do the traditional kind of promotion behind it

431
00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:24.070
and realizing like, you couldn't get up for it.

432
00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:26.100
Like I just can't do that.

433
00:20:26.100 --> 00:20:26.933
Yeah.

434
00:20:26.933 --> 00:20:28.480
And the obstacles there being,

435
00:20:28.480 --> 00:20:31.210
like all of these people who are so heavily invested

436
00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:33.215
in the success of this music,

437
00:20:33.215 --> 00:20:36.610
it took a lot of gumption and courage

438
00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:39.050
to opt out of that and say, I'm not gonna do that.

439
00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:40.330
I'm gonna do this other thing.

440
00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:41.410
And I'm sure there were a lot of people

441
00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:43.684
who weren't very happy about that at the time.

442
00:20:43.684 --> 00:20:46.330
Yeah, I'm not sure if we covered it last time.

443
00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:48.110
You could, I don't know if you remember either,

444
00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:49.143
it was a while ago but-

445
00:20:49.143 --> 00:20:50.540
I didn't go back and listen to it.

446
00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:51.623
We probably did talk about it but.

447
00:20:51.623 --> 00:20:56.623
But yeah, I was, I had the dream of doing it

448
00:20:56.850 --> 00:20:58.870
like five years.

449
00:20:58.870 --> 00:21:01.310
And you're right.

450
00:21:01.310 --> 00:21:04.840
I felt like I was just caught under the weight

451
00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:06.320
of my own life.

452
00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:09.030
And I had done all the research

453
00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:10.490
about the walk across America.

454
00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:12.460
It turns out there's a strategy to it.

455
00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:14.510
Best to start east to west

456
00:21:14.510 --> 00:21:16.970
'cause of where the mountain ranges line up.

457
00:21:16.970 --> 00:21:20.370
And best to start in spring, early spring

458
00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:23.022
in an effort to be done before winter.

459
00:21:23.022 --> 00:21:25.070
So each time spring rolled around

460
00:21:25.070 --> 00:21:26.060
it was something in the way.

461
00:21:26.060 --> 00:21:26.893
Right.

462
00:21:26.893 --> 00:21:28.300
It's an album I gotta finish.

463
00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:31.157
There's a tour I gotta do to support the last album.

464
00:21:31.157 --> 00:21:32.880
Its never gonna be convenient.

465
00:21:32.880 --> 00:21:34.610
There's a wedding I got to go to.

466
00:21:34.610 --> 00:21:39.220
And I just didn't do it,

467
00:21:39.220 --> 00:21:41.190
five years I was letting my dream die

468
00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:43.523
and I felt it, man.

469
00:21:43.523 --> 00:21:46.820
It's like I started to have this low-level depression

470
00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:48.360
kind of creep into my life.

471
00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:51.570
And I was talking to another guy,

472
00:21:51.570 --> 00:21:54.560
I think we have in common, Elliot Bisnow.

473
00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:57.270
Sure, Elliot and I went to the same high school.

474
00:21:57.270 --> 00:21:58.103
Is that right?

475
00:21:58.103 --> 00:21:59.956
Yeah.
How about that?

476
00:21:59.956 --> 00:22:00.860
So I was talking to Elliot-

477
00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:02.330
Julie talks to Elliot all the time.

478
00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:05.020
Amazing, yeah, he's another guy

479
00:22:05.020 --> 00:22:08.380
who just exudes superhuman enthusiasm.

480
00:22:08.380 --> 00:22:10.220
So I said, let me talk to him

481
00:22:10.220 --> 00:22:13.070
'cause I feel utterly uninspired

482
00:22:13.920 --> 00:22:16.463
and maybe his positivity will like,

483
00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:20.800
through our conversation, seep into me, you know.

484
00:22:20.800 --> 00:22:22.627
And so, I told him, yeah, I was like,

485
00:22:22.627 --> 00:22:25.460
dude, I just can't do this anymore.

486
00:22:25.460 --> 00:22:28.097
This whole like Mike Posner show going on the road.

487
00:22:28.097 --> 00:22:32.060
You know, doing the shows, yeah, put your hands up.

488
00:22:32.060 --> 00:22:33.493
I can't do it.

489
00:22:35.240 --> 00:22:37.073
He goes, well, what do you wanna do.

490
00:22:38.530 --> 00:22:41.040
I said, what I really wanna do is walk across America,

491
00:22:41.040 --> 00:22:43.890
but I told my manager, they all think is crazy.

492
00:22:43.890 --> 00:22:45.803
He goes, that's great news!

493
00:22:47.350 --> 00:22:49.200
And I'm like, what do you mean.

494
00:22:49.200 --> 00:22:51.400
That they think it's crazy, it's great news.

495
00:22:52.310 --> 00:22:53.610
So I'm confused.

496
00:22:53.610 --> 00:22:56.950
I'm like, what are you talking about.

497
00:22:56.950 --> 00:22:59.030
He goes, you gotta understand,

498
00:22:59.030 --> 00:23:01.950
not all crazy ideas are great,

499
00:23:01.950 --> 00:23:04.323
but all great ideas are crazy.

500
00:23:05.340 --> 00:23:10.053
And I think you walking across America is a great idea.

501
00:23:11.431 --> 00:23:12.264
And that was it.

502
00:23:12.264 --> 00:23:13.097
He told me that.
And you gotta live

503
00:23:13.097 --> 00:23:14.230
your life, man.
I felt it.

504
00:23:14.230 --> 00:23:15.230
I felt it like the-

505
00:23:15.230 --> 00:23:16.260
Dream deferred.

506
00:23:16.260 --> 00:23:20.090
I could feel the truth underneath what he was saying,

507
00:23:20.090 --> 00:23:21.970
and it was just like,

508
00:23:21.970 --> 00:23:23.780
there's never gonna be a right time.

509
00:23:23.780 --> 00:23:25.760
No one's gonna roll out a red carpet for me.

510
00:23:25.760 --> 00:23:26.880
People are always gonna have a reason

511
00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:28.350
why I shouldn't do this.

512
00:23:28.350 --> 00:23:29.800
You're gonna hurt your body.

513
00:23:29.800 --> 00:23:32.650
You're gonna, like your career's gonna suffer.

514
00:23:32.650 --> 00:23:35.610
I'd heard them all, but it was like, this is my life.

515
00:23:35.610 --> 00:23:36.680
And I'm either gonna live it,

516
00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:38.480
like this is either gonna be a part of my life,

517
00:23:38.480 --> 00:23:41.210
this walk, this dream, or I'm gonna live

518
00:23:41.210 --> 00:23:42.840
some other like crappy version

519
00:23:42.840 --> 00:23:44.480
that I know isn't my truth.

520
00:23:44.480 --> 00:23:45.313
Right.

521
00:23:45.313 --> 00:23:48.270
But there's also this idea of what the walk

